## Black-texel counts

Method: read `out/storytime-nut/textures/baseColor.png`, take texels with maximum channel at or
below 24, and keep those with at least five of eight painted neighbours, so the empty gutter does
not count as a speck. Script kept outside the repository (`/tmp/opencode/blacktex.mjs`).

| Build | Triangles | Black texels | Note |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Batch 8, commit `d6d9f5b9` | 2,266 | 90 | dotted specks and a 4 mm dashed seam line |
| Option 1: `maxError` 0.00004, `maxTriangles` 8000 | 5,698 | 111 | seam line left, one stroke appeared on the back |
| Option 2: option 1 plus rounder tip and larger fillets | 5,374 | 91 | cap edge clean, three hairline strokes on the side cap top |
| Option 3: `texture: false` (vertex colors) | 5,894 | not applicable | no atlas is written |

## Option that worked

Option 3, vertex colors. `texture: false`, `paintWeight: 1`, and a paint blend of 0.0015 m for the
soft cap boundary. The body keeps the 0.0045 m union, the 0.005 m cap lobe fillet, and the thicker
stem tip from option 2. `maxError` 0.00004 m and `maxTriangles` 8000 keep the crease and the stem.
The texture atlas and the `bump` went away, because both need a bake.

## src/ follow-up for routing (no src/ change made)

`src/texture/bake.ts` lines 150 to 158 take one Newton step from the reduced-mesh point onto the
surface. Far from the surface, or where the gradient is weak, the step lands off the surface. The
paint blend cannot return pure black from the three palette colors, so a pure black texel means a
failed sample. Evidence: 90 to 111 pure black texels inside the charts of three builds, each one
surrounded by painted texels.

